SUMMARY:YOW launch · Approve the calendar and reserve daily evening review blocks through 30 N...
DESCRIPTION:WHAT THIS MEANS\nCreate one stable starting version of the app. We first prove the current code can build and pass its automatic checks before adding more launch work.\n\nEXACTLY WHAT TO DO\n1. Open this workbook and stay on this row. Do not work ahead.\n2. Open Codex. Copy the entire prompt from the next column and send it unchanged.\n3. Wait for Codex to give you one step. If it gives several steps\, ask it to give you only the first one.\n4. Complete today's owner action: Approve the calendar and reserve daily evening review blocks through 30 November.\n5. Safety rule: Do not run terminal commands\, edit code\, or change production settings yourself. Codex handles technical work and explains any owner-only click before you make it.\n6. After every click or decision\, tell Codex exactly what appeared on screen. If it differs from the instruction\, stop instead of guessing.\n7. At the end\, ask: “What evidence proves this passed\, and did you update the roadmap?”\n8. Set Status to Done only if Codex confirms the result and evidence. Otherwise choose In progress or Blocked and paste the reason into Notes.\n\nCOPY INTO CODEX\nToday is 2026-09-28. I am a complete beginner and I am following the YOW paid-launch plan. My only task today is: Approve the calendar and reserve daily evening review blocks through 30 November. The result we need is: Freeze launch scope and classify every remaining item as launch-blocking\, verification-only\, or post-launch. Guide me through this one step at a time. Before every step\, tell me: (1) which app or website to open\, (2) exactly what to click or type\, (3) what I should expect to see\, and (4) what I must not touch. Do not ask me to edit code or run terminal commands\; do that work yourself. Use safe test accounts and disposable data. Stop before any destructive\, production\, billing\, email\, or public action and explain it in plain English. Wait for my reply after each step. At the end\, tell me whether to mark this Done\, In progress\, or Blocked\, and record the evidence in the roadmap.\n\nDONE MEANS\nFreeze launch scope and classify every remaining item as launch-blocking\, verification-only\, or post-launch.\nCodex confirms the evidence was recorded and tells you to mark Done.\n\nHARD GATE\nYes
CATEGORIES:YOW Launch\,Release baseline\,Week 1
TRANSP:OPAQUE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
